From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:36:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 49/55] perf(ws): compress the canvas room's messages with
 permessage-deflate

ws leaves permessage-deflate off. The canvas reaches the editor as one
init message holding every page's frames with their HTML: 5.7 MB for a
canvas of 459 frames. On a shaped 4G link (60 ms RTT, 9 Mbit/s down)
that took about five seconds to arrive, the stage empty all the while.

Frame HTML compresses well across frames: 5.1 MB of it to 312 KB at
zlib's default level and window, in about 65 ms on the zlib thread
pool (not the event loop). A smaller window loses most of that (1.4 MB
at 12 bits, about 2 MB at 10), so the window stays at 15. With no
context takeover each message is compressed on its own and a
connection keeps no history between messages; ws sends messages under
1 KB (cursors, presence) uncompressed.

First load of that canvas over the shaped 4G link with a 4x CPU
slowdown, four interleaved runs each: frames on screen at 5.4-6.2 s
compressed against 10.0-10.8 s uncompressed; everything in view shown
at 6.0-7.0 s against 10.7-11.5 s. Browsers have negotiated the
extension for over a decade; a client that does not offer it gets
plain frames as before.
---
 server/index.ts | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/server/index.ts b/server/index.ts
index 3e1950e..43c53bb 100644
--- a/server/index.ts
+++ b/server/index.ts
@@ -3426,7 +3426,20 @@ app.use(undoRequest)
 app.use(workBudgetRefusal)
 
 const server = http.createServer(app)
-const wss = new WebSocketServer({ server, path: '/ws' })
+/* permessage-deflate, which ws leaves off. The canvas reaches the editor as one
+   message, every page's frames with their HTML: 5.7 MB for a canvas of 459
+   frames, which a 4G connection took about five seconds to bring in, the stage
+   empty all the while. HTML compresses well across frames (to 312 KB at zlib's
+   default level and window, ~65 ms on the zlib thread pool, not the event
+   loop); a small window loses most of that (1.4 MB at 12 bits), so the window
+   stays. Without context takeover each message is compressed on its own, so a
+   connection carries no compression history between messages; ws leaves the
+   small ones (under 1 KB: cursors, presence) uncompressed. */
+const wss = new WebSocketServer({
+  server,
+  path: '/ws',
+  perMessageDeflate: { serverNoContextTakeover: true, clientNoContextTakeover: true },
+})
 
